WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.811
I did want to talk about something

00:00:02.811 --> 00:00:06.719
important here at the
very top of the show.

00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:08.960
As some of you have
heard, it's been out there

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.900
for a while now, but
we're making it official.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.650
We are winding down our TBS show.

00:00:16.011 --> 00:00:18.967
The plan is to re-emerge on HBO Max

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:20.589
sometime in the near future.

00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:25.589
with I think what will be my
fourth iteration of a program.

00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:28.647
Imagine a cooking show with puppets

00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:30.411
and you'll have the wrong idea.

00:00:30.411 --> 00:00:33.469
Anyway, we're going to
be making this switch.

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:35.400
Now, some of you are probably wondering,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.209
why am I doing this?

00:00:37.209 --> 00:00:40.119
Why end things here at TBS?

00:00:40.119 --> 00:00:43.149
And I'll tell you because
a very old Buddhist monk

00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:46.208
once told me that to pick something up

00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:49.189
you must first put something down.

00:00:49.189 --> 00:00:50.022
Yeah.

00:00:50.022 --> 00:00:50.855
Now I'll be honest with you,

00:00:50.855 --> 00:00:54.917
he was drunk out of his
skull and very belligerent

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:56.648
and I maintained, you
can pick up two things

00:00:56.648 --> 00:00:57.979
if you use both hands.

00:00:57.979 --> 00:00:59.749
He just got mad and
started swinging at me.

00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:03.091
So I ended the conversation
and took his advice.

00:01:03.091 --> 00:01:04.349
We'll be moving on.

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:08.516
Our last episode here at
TBS will be on June 24th.

00:01:10.949 --> 00:01:13.628
Now the plan is we're going to be showing

00:01:13.628 --> 00:01:15.968
a lot of clips of our favorite moments

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:17.885
from the last 11 years.

00:01:19.098 --> 00:01:21.019
We're going to have some special guests.

00:01:21.019 --> 00:01:21.852
We're going to create, I think,

00:01:21.852 --> 00:01:25.456
a really fun, special environment.

00:01:25.456 --> 00:01:28.760
And it's going to be,
I think, a lot of fun.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.819
And you know, I just want to
point out that for 11 years

00:01:32.819 --> 00:01:36.688
the people at Turner have
been absolutely lovely

00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:39.958
to me and everyone here at the staff.

00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:42.685
They gave me a home when I needed one most

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:44.498
and I am eternally grateful.

00:01:44.498 --> 00:01:47.226
I'm very proud of what
we've accomplished here.

00:01:47.226 --> 00:01:49.209
And so what I'd like is I'd like

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:52.635
these last couple of weeks
to be a fond look back

00:01:52.635 --> 00:01:56.539
at all the absurd madness that
my team and I have concocted.

00:01:56.539 --> 00:01:57.568
Best of all,

00:01:57.568 --> 00:01:59.520
I just want to point out
there will be shockingly few

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.595
if any, references to Donald Trump

00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:05.459
because that's always been
my favorite kind of comedy.

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.376
So tune in these next
two months and check out,

00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:12.825
as we say farewell to this show

00:02:12.825 --> 00:02:15.492
and move on to the next horizon.

00:02:17.317 --> 00:02:19.458
No one ever says the next horizon.

00:02:19.458 --> 00:02:21.210
It's just what came to me in the moment.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.747
Yeah, there's only one horizon.

00:02:22.747 --> 00:02:23.580
There's only one horizon.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.413
[Andy] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:26.392
I'm regretting the next horizon thing.

00:02:26.392 --> 00:02:27.371
There's just one horizon.

00:02:27.371 --> 00:02:28.204
It's all right.

00:02:28.204 --> 00:02:29.037
Yeah.

00:02:29.037 --> 00:02:29.870
I apologize.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:30.703
Right.

00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:32.373
As we head to that next mountain top, huh?

00:02:32.373 --> 00:02:33.206
That's fine.

00:02:33.206 --> 00:02:34.039
Okay.

00:02:34.039 --> 00:02:34.980
[Andy] Yeah.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:35.813
Over the horizon.

00:02:35.813 --> 00:02:37.256
Although at this point
it'll probably just be

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.750
like a slight hill.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.656
Just a small hill.

00:02:39.656 --> 00:02:40.489
[Andy] We're old.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:41.322
Yeah.

00:02:41.322 --> 00:02:42.155
[Andy] Yeah.

00:02:42.155 --> 00:02:43.579
I don't want to go up a mountain anymore.

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:45.835
I'm too old for that.

00:02:45.835 --> 00:02:46.798
It'll be a slight rise.

00:02:46.798 --> 00:02:47.631
Right.

00:02:47.631 --> 00:02:51.376
And I'll be on one of those electric,

00:02:51.376 --> 00:02:53.136
electric scooters you
see people in the mall

00:02:53.136 --> 00:02:54.747
driving around in, yeah.

00:02:54.747 --> 00:02:55.776
Cresting.

00:02:55.776 --> 00:02:58.136
Anyway, so watch for that.

00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:00.787
And we'll be talking a lot
about it in the weeks to come.

00:03:00.787 --> 00:03:04.537
I just wanted to give
you a little heads up.

